## المرحلة 1: أساسيات المحادثة

### P1.1 الرد والتعديل والحذف والنسخ

```text
Feature: Reply, edit, delete, copy.
Attached: chat view, message bubble, composer, TDLib service files.
Requirements:
- Long-press (context menu) on a message: Reply, Edit (own messages only), Delete (for me / for everyone when allowed), Copy.
- Show a reply preview bar above the composer and a quoted preview inside the bubble; tapping it scrolls to the original message.
- Edited messages show an "edited" label. React to updateMessageEdited and updateDeleteMessages.
Done when: all four actions work in private chats, groups, and channels where permitted.
```

### P1.2 الرسائل المحفوظة وإعادة التوجيه

```text
Feature: Saved Messages and forwarding.
Requirements:
- Saved Messages chat at the top of the chat list.
- Forward one or several selected messages to one or more chats, with an option to hide the original sender.
- Multi-select mode in chat (select, forward, delete).
Done when: forwarding a mix of text, photo, and file works.
```

### P1.3 المجلدات والأرشيف والكتم والتثبيت

```text
Feature: Chat folders, archive, mute, pin.
Requirements:
- Folder tabs above the chat list from TDLib chat folders (list, create, edit, reorder, delete).
- Archive list via the archive chat list, with swipe actions: archive, mute (duration choices), pin, mark read/unread.
- Pinned chats stay on top per list. Unread badges per folder.
Done when: folder changes sync with the official Telegram app on my account.
```

### P1.4 الإشعارات

```text
Feature: Push notifications design and client side.
Goal: Explain the options, then implement the client side.
Requirements:
- Explain clearly that APNs push for a third-party Telegram client needs a server that receives pushes and relays them, and what that server must do with TDLib's registerDevice / processPushNotification flow.
- Implement client side: permission request, device token registration with TDLib, local notifications while the app runs, per-chat notification settings screen, badge count.
- Do not build the server yet; give me a short design for it.
Done when: foreground and local notifications work and the push flow is documented.
```

